    extendedIntro: "An all in one wedding invitation should feel effortless for guests, even when it holds a great deal of information. It is the one place they can return to for the celebration, RSVP, schedule, travel guidance and later memories. Rather than adding features for their own sake, shape every section around a real guest need: receiving the news, deciding whether they can attend, finding the venue and preparing for the day. When the visual and practical details share one calm system, the invitation becomes a thoughtful extension of the celebration—not another task for guests to manage.",
    closingGuide: "Before you publish, read the invitation as each kind of guest would. A close friend may only need the RSVP and dinner time. A family member travelling from another country may need the schedule, airport, hotel area and dress code. Someone unable to attend may want a way to leave a note and later view approved memories. This final pass often reveals where a label is unclear, a detail is buried or a link needs testing. It is also the right time to check the experience on different screen sizes, because most guests will first encounter the invitation on a phone. Keep the words warm but direct; guests should never need to guess what is happening or what they need to do. When the essentials are easy, the design has room to feel special. FOLDÈ Wedding gives couples a polished starting point for this guest journey, but the most successful invitation is always shaped by the care you put into the people receiving it.",
